{"instance_id": "AzureAD__microsoft-authentication-library-for-python-454", "repo": "AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-python", "category": "Performance Issue", "issue": "MSAL can consider using lazy import for `request`, `jwt`\n**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nImporting MSAL is can cost ~300ms on Windows due to some heavy libraries like `request` and `jwt`: \r\n\r\n```\r\npython -X importtime -c \"import msal\"  2>perf.log; tuna .\\perf.log\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4003950/137872368-a85b9753-f46b-4ffe-acdd-323815486c1b.png)\r\n\r\nMSAL can consider using lazy import for these libraries so that importing MSAL can be lightweight. (Azure CLI lazily imports MSAL: https://github.com/Azure/azure-cli/pull/19898)\n", "gold": ["msal/authority.py"], "hybrid_top": [{"file": "msal/application.py"}, {"file": "msal/authority.py"}, {"file": "sample/vault_jwt_sample.py"}, {"file": "msal/oauth2cli/authcode.py"}, {"file": "msal/region.py"}, {"file": "msal/oauth2cli/oauth2.py"}, {"file": "msal/token_cache.py"}, {"file": "msal/wstrust_request.py"}, {"file": "msal/oauth2cli/assertion.py"}, {"file": "msal/__init__.py"}, {"file": ".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.md"}, {"file": "msal/oauth2cli/http.py"}, {"file": "msal/telemetry.py"}, {"file": "msal/individual_cache.py"}, {"file": "msal/oauth2cli/oidc.py"}, {"file": "sample/interactive_sample.py"}, {"file": "msal/throttled_http_client.py"}, {"file": "sample/confidential_client_secret_sample.py"}, {"file": "sample/confidential_client_certificate_sample.py"}, {"file": "msal/oauth2cli/__init__.py"}, {"file": "sample/username_password_sample.py"}, {"file": "msal/mex.py"}, {"file": "setup.py"}, {"file": "msal/wstrust_response.py"}, {"file": "sample/device_flow_sample.py"}, {"file": "msal/exceptions.py"}, {"file": "sample/migrate_rt.py"}, {"file": "contributing.md"}, {"file": "sample/authorization-code-flow-sample/authorization_code_flow_sample.py"}, {"file": "README.md"}, {"file": ".github/workflows/python-package.yml"}, {"file": "setup.cfg"}, {"file": ".travis.yml"}, {"file": "requirements.txt"}, {"file": "tests/test_e2e.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_authority.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_application.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_throttled_http_client.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_client.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_token_cache.py"}, {"file": "docs/index.rst"}, {"file": "tests/test_ccs.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_authcode.py"}, {"file": "docs/conf.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_individual_cache.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_wstrust.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_assertion.py"}, {"file": "tests/__init__.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_authority_patch.py"}, {"file": "tests/http_client.py"}, {"file": "tests/test_mex.py"}]}
{"instance_id": "CWorthy-ocean__roms-tools-227", "repo": "CWorthy-ocean/roms-tools", "category": "Performance Issue", "issue": "Radiation correction is not done in parallel (even when using Dask)\n## Issue\n\nIf the user chooses to apply a radiation correction for the surface forcing while using Dask via\n```\nSurfaceForcing(\n    grid=grid,\n    ...,\n    correct_radiation=True,\n    use_dask=True\n)\n```\nthis radiation correction is not done in parallel. The reason for this is the internal use of the function \nhttps://github.com/CWorthy-ocean/roms-tools/blob/67df5fc400b1daeb903ba9b2efe11899d8b55dfa/roms_tools/setup/utils.py#L128-L150\n\nwhich interpolates a pre-computed climatology for ERA5 shortwave downward radiation (i.e., 12 time stamps) to the hourly ERA5 data of interest. Specifically, this line is the issue:\n\nhttps://github.com/CWorthy-ocean/roms-tools/blob/67df5fc400b1daeb903ba9b2efe11899d8b55dfa/roms_tools/setup/utils.py#L184-L187\n\nBoth `data_array_concat` and `day_of_year` are chunked in time with chunk size 1, where `data_array_concat.time` has a length of 12 + 2, and `day_of_year.time` a length of however many ERA5 times there are: for a month of ERA5 data, that is 744 hourly time slices, i.e., 744 time chunks. However, the `xarray.interp` function cannot deal with chunked data along the core dimension and will return interpolated data with a single time chunk (containing 744 time slices). This means that this operation is not done in parallel.\n\nNote that substituting this by something like\n```\n        data_array_interpolated = xr.apply_ufunc(\n            np.interp, \n            day_of_year, \n       ", "gold": ["roms_tools/setup/datasets.py", "roms_tools/setup/surface_forcing.py", "roms_tools/setup/utils.py"], "hybrid_top": [{"file": "roms_tools/setup/utils.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/surface_forcing.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/datasets.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/boundary_forcing.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/tides.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/initial_conditions.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/fill.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/grid.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/utils.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/analysis/roms_output.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/river_forcing.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/topography.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/regrid.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/nesting.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/__init__.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/download.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/vertical_coordinate.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/plot.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/mask.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/setup/__init__.py"}, {"file": ".github/workflows/pypipublish.yaml"}, {"file": "README.md"}, {"file": "pyproject.toml"}, {"file": ".pre-commit-config.yaml"}, {"file": ".github/workflows/pre-commit.yaml"}, {"file": ".github/pull_request_template.md"}, {"file": ".github/workflows/sphinx.yaml"}, {"file": "coverage.toml"}, {"file": ".readthedocs.yaml"}, {"file": "ci/environment.yml"}, {"file": ".github/PULL_RELEASE_TEMPLATE.md"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_surface_forcing.py"}, {"file": "conftest.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_boundary_forcing.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_datasets.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_initial_conditions.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_grid.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_utils.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_river_forcing.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_tides.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_validation.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_nesting.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_analysis/test_roms_output.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_regrid.py"}, {"file": "docs/conf.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_topography.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/test_fill.py"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_utils.py"}, {"file": "docs/methods.md"}, {"file": ".github/workflows/tests.yaml"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/test_setup/__init__.py"}, {"file": "docs/releases.md"}, {"file": "roms_tools/tests/__init__.py"}, {"file": "docs/datasets.md"}, {"file": "docs/installation.rst"}, {"file": "docs/index.rst"}, {"file": "docs/api.rst"}, {"file": "docs/contributing.rst"}, {"file": "docs/environment.yml"}, {"file": "docs/_templates/autosummary/class.rst"}]}
